# Line endings.
#
# Committed files in this repo carry mixed line endings and dev machines run core.autocrlf=true, so
# a file committed CRLF and rewritten by a tool that emits bare LF churns its entire diff.
#
# package-lock.json is the one that matters: npm generates it, it is over 10,000 lines, it is
# committed all-CRLF, and every tool that regenerates it writes bare LF. Dependabot does, which
# turned a single indirect version bump into a +10807/-10834 whole-file diff with 33 real lines
# inside it. Pin the file to LF so the committed blob matches what npm writes and a dependency
# diff shows only the versions that changed.
#
# Scoped to this file on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto` would rewrite the 87 files that are
# already committed with mixed endings, which is a churn commit in its own right.
package-lock.json text eol=lf
